   section 'Conquests by Northern Peoples':
      In 1127, the [[Jurchen people|Jurchens]], a people from the northeast, captured [[Kaifeng]] and [[Jingkang incident|took the Song emperor prisoner]]. In 1194, the Yellow River [[Changes in the course of the Yellow River|changed its course]], flowing southward 
