      The wars of the late Ming and early [[Qing dynasty|Qing]] (circa 1630–1662) once again devastated Henan. During the [[Kangxi Emperor|Kangxi]] reign, the province's agricultural economy recovered, and it gradually regained its status as a major population cente
      On September 30, 1887, a major Yellow River dike breach occurred at Xiayun Shibao in Zhengzhou (present-day Shiqiao Village, [[Huayuankou, Henan|Huayuankou]] Town, Huiji District). The disaster claimed over two million lives (with estimates ranging from 930,00
