      The Islamization of Xinjiang started around 1000 AD. Xinjiang Muslim [[Turkic peoples]] contain Uyghurs, Kazaks, Kyrgyz, [[Tatars]], [[Uzbeks]]; Muslim [[Iranian peoples]] comprise Tajiks, [[Tajiks of Xinjiang|Sarikolis]] / [[Wakhi people|Wakhis]] (often confl
      The Han Chinese of Xinjiang arrived at different times from different directions and social backgrounds. There are now descendants of criminals and officials who had been exiled from China during the second half of the 18th and the first half of the 19th centu
      [[File:Xinjiang County-Level Ethnicity Map (2018 data).svg|thumb|left|[[County-level division|County-level]] ethnicity map of Xinjiang as of 2018]]
      In 2002, there were 9,632,600 males (growth rate of 1.0 percent) and 9,419,300 females (growth rate of 2.2 percent). The population overall growth rate was 1.09 percent, with 1.63 percent of [[birth rate]] and 0.54 percent [[mortality rate]].
